    "caption": "Perfect to welcome the Easter weekend with, this Easter Egg Nest Cake — made with none other than Cadbury Dairy Milk Top Deck Easter Eggs — is the ultimate chocolate cake for the season.\n\nRich, decadent, and topped with fun Cadbury Eggs, celebrate Easter Sunday with this delicious and chocolatey dessert. Find all the ingredients you need, including your favorite Cadbury confectionery, at #TheMarketplace!\n\nServing Time: 1 hour and 30 minutes\nYield: 6-8 servings\n\nIngredients\n\n1 cup semi-sweet chocolate, chopped\n½ cup butter\n1 ½ tsp. vanilla extract\n4 egg whites\n1 cup white sugar\n4 egg yolks\n2 whole eggs\n1 cup whipping cream\n½ cup confectioners’ sugar\n2 cups Cadbury Dairy Milk Top Deck Easter eggs\n\nProcedure\n\n1. Preheat oven to 180°C. \n2. In a double boiler, melt semi-sweet chocolate and butter while stirring continuously to avoid burning. Mix in 1 tsp. vanilla extract. Let cool and set aside.\n3. In a stand mixer, whip egg whites until foamy. Gradually add in ⅔ cup of white sugar, and whip until medium peaks. \n4. In another bowl, whisk together egg yolks, whole eggs, and the remaining sugar. Mix in melted chocolate mixture. \n5. Carefully fold in whipped egg whites into the chocolate egg yolk mixture. Do this in batches to avoid deflating the egg whites to much.\n6. Transfer to an 8 inch springform pan, and bake for 38-40 minutes. \n7. In the meantime, whip the whipping cream with confectioners’ sugar and the remaining vanilla extract. Whip until medium peaks.\n8. Once the cake has cooled, top with whipped cream and Cadbury Dairy Milk Top Deck Easter eggs.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
