    "campaign": "EASTER",
    "caption": "A play on the famous Key Lime Pie made with the freshest, juiciest kiwis from #TheMarketplace, this Kiwi Lime Pie is bursting with zesty citrus flavors, balanced out by the refreshing sweetness from kiwis.\n\nThe trick here is to bake the crust properly, and the simple combination of graham crackers, pecans, and butter for the base creates a solid flavor foundation for the fruity topping.\n\nServe this during your Easter lunch and enjoy!\n\nServing Time: 2 hours and 40 minutes\nYield: 6-8 servings\n\nIngredients\n\n2 cups graham crackers\n⅓ cup pecans\n3 tbsps. white sugar\n½ cup butter, melted\n½ tsp. salt\n½ cup lime juice\n3 tbsps. lime zest\n2 cans condensed milk\n2 eggs\n1½ cups whipped cream \n4 pcs. Kiwi, peeled and sliced\n\nProcedure\n\n1. Preheat oven to 175°C.\n2. In a food processor, combine graham crackers, pecans, sugar, butter and salt. Pulse until crackers and nuts are well crushed, and the mixture is sandy. \n3. Transfer to an 8-inch pie pan. Spread evenly, and pack the graham mixture up to the sides to create a border. Bake for 10 minutes, then let cool and set aside.\n4. In a stand mixer, combine lime juice, 1 tbsp. lime zest, condensed milk and eggs. Whip until thick, about 5 minutes. \n5. Transfer the egg mixture into the baked crust, and bake again for 12-15 minutes, or until set.\n6. Refrigerate for at least two hours. \n7. Once chilled, top with whipped cream, sliced Kiwi and the remaining lime zest.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
