    "caption": "Because Easter is the season that celebrates all things “egg”, here’s an elevated take on the classic egg salad made with Gemsun Sunny’s Brown Eggs.\n\nFor this French-Style Egg Salad, the mixture comes served on a bed of arugula and on top of sourdough bread. The punchy greens lift the creamy egg salad, adding more contrast and oomph to its classic counterpart.\n\nFind Gemsun Sunny’s Brown Eggs at #TheMarketplace, make this on Easter Sunday, and hear everyone around the table say “ooh-la-la”! You’ll never make egg salad the same way again.\n\nServing Time: 20 minutes\nYield: 6 servings\n\nIngredients\n\n6 pcs. Gemsun Sunny’s Brown Eggs \n¼ cup mayonnaise \n3 tbsps. dijon mustard \n1 tbsp. parsley, chopped\n3 tbsps. spring onions, chopped\nSalt and pepper to taste\n6 slices sourdough bread \n3 tbsps. olive oil\n2 cups arugula\n\nProcedure\n\n1. Boil Gemsun Sunny’s Brown Eggs for 10 minutes. Drain, and place in an ice bath to stop the cooking. \n2. Peel and roughly chop cooked eggs into bite size pieces, then set aside. \n3. In a large bowl, combine mayonnaise, dijon mustard, parsley and 1 tbsp. spring onions. Mix in chopped eggs. Season with salt and pepper to taste. Chill while toasting the bread.\n4. Spread olive oil on sourdough bread slices, then toast until crisp. \n5. Pile arugula on each bread slice, then top with egg salad. Garnish with spring onions. \n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
